sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Session as REPL / session core
    participant DepSvc as Dependency service
    participant Packet as Dep work packet
    participant Store as Compiler-owned publication store
    participant Sched as CompileScheduler
    participant Worker as Worker subsystem

    Note over Session,Worker: Target state: one authority owns dependency publication, registration, wait, and resume.

    alt Session or worker discovers dependency
        Session->>DepSvc: ensure_dependency(dep)
    else Worker->>DepSvc: ensure_dependency(dep)
    end

    DepSvc->>Store: publish dep payload once
    DepSvc->>Packet: create dep work packet
    DepSvc->>Sched: register or join existing dep work
    DepSvc->>Sched: block/wait using one canonical protocol

    Sched->>Worker: dispatch dep work packet
    Worker->>Store: consume packet / read published dep payload
    Worker->>Store: publish completed symbol/module state
    Worker->>Sched: notify typecheck done / unblock waiters

    Sched-->>DepSvc: dep ready
    DepSvc-->>Session: resume caller

    Note over DepSvc: Sole publish-before-register authority.
    Note over Store,Sched: Publication barrier and readiness observation are coupled through one protocol, not mirrored paths.
    Note over Worker: Workers consume packets rather than reconstructing the protocol from ambient shared maps.
